  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1240 PM MDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nLong-range forecast remains on track, with the upper high expected \nto build back in over the Four Corners Region. This will amplify the \nupper ridge, leading to drier conditions across the area through \nmost of the week. After much drier conditions on Tuesday, lingering \nlow to mid-level moisture will allow for more scattered thunderstorm \nactivity each day. Storms will first form over the mountains, with a \npassing front on Wednesday bringing precipitation back to the plains \nas well. Meanwhile, high temps will increase across the board, with \nhigh-80s over the valleys and high-90s over the eastern plains, with \na low but non-zero chance for some more triple digits heading into \nthis weekend.",
